#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b111120-41dd-5a58-bcc5-b0b6fc78b384" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Sides of a Polygon Given the Sum of Its Interior Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f8c4f4d-a7cb-5f36-ba29-a840d9bbe587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548564} {:answer/id #uuid "ae31482c-97e7-5e10-8bf9-1fb019613501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548700} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5c0925-8ebb-5ac7-b69a-43148347d1bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548752} {:answer/id #uuid "ef70b68e-e007-52ca-93c9-efe7e0c22ece" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548828} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c3f901-4de5-5726-95e7-07fe74a05efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca5c0925-8ebb-5ac7-b69a-43148347d1bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548752} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8f0acf3-60c9-5fe9-a760-cefa37eb9b66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "918f9202-d934-535a-b14f-29131ec63f3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-118069" :question/problem "The sum of the interior angles of a polygon is ${3960}^{∘}.$ How many sides does it have?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the sum of the interior angles of a polygon with $n$ sides is ${180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2).$\n\nTo find the number of sides in our polygon, we start by setting up the following equation:\n\n$$\n{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2)=3\\,{960}^{∘}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $n,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & =3\\,{960}^{∘} \\\\ n-2 & =\\frac{3\\,{960}^{∘}}{{180}^{∘}} \\\\ n-2 & =22 \\\\ n & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polygon has $n=24$ sides."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bad93a16-17d4-50ff-89c8-f3d966df5f1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Quantities in Quadrilaterals and Pentagons"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc54541-63d3-5382-8d61-ad8fb7a2df0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548386} {:answer/id #uuid "55f686c3-4dc7-5ee6-94df-392ace9f44b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548516} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ab1399-f698-5779-856e-01b204aa3767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548680} {:answer/id #uuid "b20abdd4-a291-58d8-b13c-b588f3c268d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{34}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548708} {:answer/id #uuid "b25b8a4a-c870-5c94-9647-8973446f4945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{68}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55f686c3-4dc7-5ee6-94df-392ace9f44b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548516} :answer-field/id #uuid "c276b696-0a88-550f-b1ad-bf6a66980d06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1f1caf2-8ee2-5aae-ae77-233643724815" :question/math-academy-id "q-4231" :question/problem "![](images/48/48d9d8513f45b87f9deffeffcef31e49a6dcaba0b033c91a918c1d72d87eb215.png)\n\nIn the quadrilateral $ABCD$ above, determine the measure of $∠C.$" :question/worked-solution "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides. Therefore, the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral  must be \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding up the internal angles and solving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C+m∠D & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x+{90}^{∘}+3x+6x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 10x+{90}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 10x & ={270}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={27}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠C & =3x \\\\  & =3({27}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={81}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bad93a16-17d4-50ff-89c8-f3d966df5f1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Quantities in Quadrilaterals and Pentagons"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23ba891b-8c25-5525-b032-ab5b189de223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548425} {:answer/id #uuid "779f08b8-d128-5006-babf-2a4ce92fda54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{8}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548574} {:answer/id #uuid "78305b75-af32-5483-8ec7-da87251e1870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{14}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548577} {:answer/id #uuid "8845496d-a3e1-5e36-8bf1-e36d44baa191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548617} {:answer/id #uuid "c14baac9-826a-5be1-a8d3-292463298b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "779f08b8-d128-5006-babf-2a4ce92fda54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{8}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548574} :answer-field/id #uuid "172b1f55-032f-506f-a1f3-de37620daea9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d216a5f-ca4b-530d-81c3-76f09a214af9" :question/math-academy-id "q-4316" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa797de4c7edfb4e4c4bc4eab40e8443f832c0407f08fd9d9ae28730c468a71e.png)\n\nIn the quadrilateral $OMNP$ shown above, find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides. Therefore, the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral must be \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding up the internal angles and solving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠O+m∠M+m∠N+m∠P & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {93}^{∘}+(14x-{7}^{∘})+(11x-{2}^{∘})+{76}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 25x+{160}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 25x & ={200}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={8}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
